WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:02.330
- [Narrator] After weeks
of intense fighting,

00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:04.610
resulting in battered
equipment and logistical issues

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:07.140
in the capital of Kyiv
and other northern cities,

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.592
Russian forces changed tack.

00:00:09.592 --> 00:00:14.342
(Volodymyr speaking in foreign language)

00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:16.320
- [Narrator] The Donbas region,

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:17.920
with flat countryside terrain,

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:19.450
is a more familiar battleground

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:20.700
for Russia's military,

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:22.210
which has trained a large portion

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:24.399
of its forces in open-air combat.

00:00:24.399 --> 00:00:25.380
(gun booming)

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.070
And its landscape is more suited

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:29.680
to conventional battles,
involving artillery systems.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:31.700
Moscow is estimated to have thousands

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:33.730
of tanks already deployed in the region

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:35.030
where Russian-led separatists

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:37.440
have been waging war since 2014.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.890
- To a large degree, it is tank country.

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:44.260
That is you can really conduct
mechanized warfare operations

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:46.807
that is really the types of operations

00:00:46.807 --> 00:00:49.231
that the Russian armed
forces traditionally

00:00:49.231 --> 00:00:51.010
are quite good at.

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:52.840
- [Narrator] The move
comes after Russian forces

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:55.970
face several setbacks in
cities across the country.

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:58.620
Among the key issues, failing
to establish dominance

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:00.500
in the skies and not preparing

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:02.860
for stiff resistance
from Ukrainian fighters,

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:04.223
military experts say.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:08.050
So as Russia shifts its
approach to focus on the east,

00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:10.800
we analyze what went
wrong for Moscow in Kyiv

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:12.550
and why it believes it can succeed

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:14.053
in this next phase of war.

00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:18.350
These images show a
convoy of Russian tanks,

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:20.940
infantry-fighting vehicles,
self-propelled artillery,

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:22.940
and logistical support heading toward Kyiv

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:24.420
in late February.

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:27.440
The column was thwarted by
Ukrainian resistance efforts

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:29.790
just days after Moscow began its invasion

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:30.980
of its smaller neighbor.

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:32.440
- Part of Russia's biggest failure

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:34.610
to take Kyiv was that
it stuck to the roads,

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:36.053
as military analysts say.

00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:39.790
Satellite imagery showed
us these large columns,

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:41.090
long columns of tanks

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:45.280
and armored vehicles going
for kilometers and miles

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:46.720
on these roads.

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:48.710
And Ukraine did a really good job

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:50.640
of ambushing them from the forests

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:52.100
and from the sky with drones.

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:53.510
- [Narrator] Striking
the long supply lines

00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:55.470
created logistical problems for Russia

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:58.430
as it tried to support its
forces inside the country.

00:01:58.430 --> 00:02:00.280
- Russian forces at the
front were struggling

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:03.000
to get basic things like
even food and water,

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.330
let alone equipment.

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:06.090
- [Narrator] Early Russian
advances to take control

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:08.220
of the capital and other northern cities

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:10.210
were also hampered by poor tactics,

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:11.640
according to analysts.

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:14.283
- They haven't really trained
for it on a large scale.

00:02:14.283 --> 00:02:15.530
The Russian armed forces

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:18.560
are essentially an
artillery army supported

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:19.970
by mechanized forces,

00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:22.580
that is tanks and other armored vehicles.

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:24.790
So they always were short on infantry

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:26.320
because the way they fight,

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:27.610
they're not really meant to go

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:31.320
into cities and conduct
urban combat operations.

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:33.070
- [Narrator] That, paired
with an unexpectedly

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:35.260
resolute defense from
the Ukrainian forces,

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:36.660
armed with nimbler weapons,

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:38.570
including Turkish-made armed drones

00:02:38.570 --> 00:02:41.410
and US-made javelins
left Russia vulnerable

00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:45.300
in the city, and saw their
forces retreat in late March.

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:46.970
Russian officials have pushed back

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:48.800
against Western and Ukrainian claims

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:50.420
that it has failed.

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:51.800
- I don't think we failed, frankly.

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:54.570
We conduct our military
operation, it's not a war,

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:55.550
it's a military operation.

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:59.000
It has its own strategy,
it has its own aims.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.190
- [Narrator] Russia's Defense Ministry

00:03:00.190 --> 00:03:02.440
didn't immediately respond
to requests for comment

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:03.773
about their changing strategy in Kyiv

00:03:03.773 --> 00:03:05.383
and the Donbas region.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:08.420
Following failures to take Kyiv,

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:10.280
Russia refocused its strategy

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:13.290
to try to take control
of the Donbas region.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:14.730
- Russia has been fighting a conflict

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:16.510
for eight years there already.

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:18.270
Pro-Russian separatists broke away

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:21.750
in two parts of the east,
Donetsk and Luhansk,

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:25.150
back in 2014 after Russia
seized Crimea from Ukraine.

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:27.420
- [Narrator] Military analysts
say controlling the region

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:29.680
and Mariupol could be key for connecting

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:31.410
what they describe as a land bridge

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:33.870
between the south of Ukraine and Russia.

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:36.430
- Uniting the east and
then southern front lines

00:03:36.430 --> 00:03:38.510
of Russian forces,

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:40.410
I think it would make it easier also

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:44.880
to resupply the Russian
troops in the south.

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:47.290
- [Narrator] There are also
environmental factors at play.

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:49.523
In contrast to Kyiv, where
dense, urban wooded areas

00:03:49.523 --> 00:03:52.000
proved difficult for Russian forces,

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:54.080
the Donbas region is more open,

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:57.180
which some analysts compare
to a World War II battlefield.

00:03:57.180 --> 00:03:58.880
If it can coordinate its forces,

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:02.130
that could allow Russia to
leverage its military equipment.

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:04.650
- The situation is a bit more advantageous

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:06.200
for the Russian armed forces,

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:08.197
but, of course, there's also some deficits

00:04:08.197 --> 00:04:09.630
and the Russians are running low

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:11.690
on precision-guided munitions.

00:04:11.690 --> 00:04:13.720
- [Narrator] And Moscow
faces a protracted fight

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:16.330
with thousands of battle-hardened
forces in the region.

00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:17.740
Analysts say Ukraine is believed

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:21.350
to have between 40 and 50,000
soldiers in the Donbas,

00:04:21.350 --> 00:04:23.190
many of whom have spent years fighting

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:24.983
against Russian-backed separatists.

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:28.660
But a big factor in who
can control this next phase

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:32.270
of war analysts say is who
can achieve air superiority,

00:04:32.270 --> 00:04:34.290
a key detail that has so far been hard

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:36.310
for open source investigators to track.

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:39.420
- You really would want
to dominate the skies

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:41.330
above your troops as they're advancing.

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:44.730
Make sure that no enemy
aircraft can attack your troops,

00:04:44.730 --> 00:04:46.530
making sure that no enemy missiles

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:47.930
can hit your troops.

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:49.410
- [Narrator] For Ukraine
to be able to withstand

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:51.270
such attacks from Russia in the east,

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:52.890
keeping the flow of advanced weapons

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:56.250
from the US and other
countries is key analysts say.

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:58.300
Ukrainian president Volodymyr Zelenskyy

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:00.610
has demanded continued
assistance from allies

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:03.500
as the country enters a
different stage of war.

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:06.190
But despite Russia's
shifting military focus,

00:05:06.190 --> 00:05:07.660
Putin's initial ambitions,

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:09.880
which Western officials said
were to take the capital

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:12.725
and install a new government
may remain missing.

00:05:12.725 --> 00:05:15.475
(dramatic music)

